WHY v3 EXISTS. v130_score_gate_v2.R applied attach_esi() to the candidate only
(line 60) and not to the baseline (line 61). attach_esi merges on STAND against
magp_qcnb_pairs.csv, which carries 126 duplicated STAND keys, so the candidate
inflated from 733 rows to 789 (in-domain 492 -> 526) while the baseline stayed at
733 / 492. Every v13.0 gate verdict from 10 July onward compared 526 duplicated
candidate rows against 492 baseline rows. THIS DEFECT WAS REAL AND REMAINS FIXED
IN v3. It is the one 11 August conclusion that survived the 12 August rebuild.

NOTHING SHIPPED. No operational AcadianGY_*.r touched. v12.10.1 remains the
shipped August version. Adoption stays a separate human decision by Aaron.
FIA true coordinates stayed on the node; aggregates only.

