NO VERSION CONFLATION EXISTS
  12.10.1 vs 12.10.2 = 3 lines: the AcadianVersionTag string, plus a .afac read of
  ops$esi.domht.afac and its use in .Aasym. Both numeric lines sit inside the block
  gated by ops$use.esi.domht, which every bench harness sets FALSE. ops$esi.domht.afac
  is assigned nowhere in the repo or on Cardinal, so .afac defaults to 1 regardless.
  The base version difference is numerically ZERO under every benched configuration.
  All three July v13.0 builds already carry AcadianVersionTag "AcadianV12.10.1".

THE REAL CAUSE OF THE 11 AUGUST NULL FAILURE
  cb_v130null_results.csv is BYTE IDENTICAL to cb_C_baonly_results.csv (BA_GAIN=1),
  max|diff| = 0 across all 29 numeric columns and 733 stands. The 11 August null
  never turned the BA lever off. bench_parity_v130_run.R does not assign
  ops$ba.anchor.gain (only bench_parity_v130_bagain.R does), so BA_GAIN=0 was
  silently ignored and the model's tryCatch default of 1 applied. The 3.63 point
  "null failure" is simply the true size of the BA correction, read with the
  candidate and baseline columns transposed.

