BAKUZIS NOW EVALUABLE (blocker cleared)
  bakuzis_allmodels.R hard-coded a missing AcadianGY_12.5.0.r. Rewired as
  scripts/phase2/bakuzis_v130.R: model set is a table of (model file, gain, coef file),
  levers carried through ops, region is a parameter. The old driver ran region ME where
  the co-fit anchor is c(1,0) by construction, so the height lever was inert and the
  test could not have detected it. Now run at NB and QC, ESI 12/16/20, to age 160.
  base_12101   all five relations PASS
  v130_baonly  all five PASS, no regression. Reineke -1.581 -> -1.619, Eichhorn CV
               10.9 -> 10.4, BA plateau 36.0 -> 34.9 m2/ha with last-20 sd 0.30 -> 0.17
  v130_honly   REGRESSION on SiteOrdering, both regions. QC: 157 height and 155 volume
               inversions of 160 ages.
  v130_both    REGRESSION on SiteOrdering, both regions, same QC magnitude.
  MECHANISM: QC co-fit ascale = 0.0193 + 0.069534*esi and dht is divided by ascale.
  ESI 12 -> ascale 0.854 (height growth up ~17%), ESI 20 -> ascale 1.410 (down ~29%).
  The slope is steep enough to invert the site gradient. NB anchor is nearly flat
  (1.10313 + 0.005844*esi) so NB shows only 1 to 2 inversions.

VERDICT
  BA net-increment anchor: REAL and defensible. Not a base-version artifact.
  Height re-anchor as fitted: DO NOT ADOPT. Degrades BA on all five subsets and
  breaks Bakuzis site ordering, catastrophically in QC.
  Joint candidate passes 4 of 5 but inherits the QC site-ordering failure.
  ADOPTION REMAINS AARON'S DECISION. Nothing shipped.

CARRY-FORWARD
  Height refit needs a monotonicity constraint on the site gradient (bound the QC slope
  or add a site-ordering penalty to the objective) before it can be re-gated.
  A tail-aware BA gain is the obvious next test for C's two volume failures at ESI_high
  and QMD_large, where the model already over-predicts volume.
  BA_GAIN above 1.0 is still inert: build_v130_baonly_v2.py clamps gain with
  min(1, max(0, gain)) and the solved scale to [0.7, 1.5]. Widen the band, not the gain.
  ME identity anchor c(1,0) still untested against data; 0 ME stands in MagPlot.
  NB_AFAC/QC_AFAC matter enormously (config F: dropping them to 1.0 moves output by
  2304 at the widest column and fails 4 of 5), so every future run must set them.
  HARNESS DEFECT STILL OPEN: bench_parity_v130_run.R silently ignores BA_GAIN. Either
  add the ops$ba.anchor.gain line to it or retire it in favour of
  bench_parity_v130_ctl.R, which reads both BA_GAIN and COEF_FILE and echoes the model
  md5 and full coefficient file into the log before every run.
